// The Six-Winged Seraph (boss id seraph): the journal, every hero in their own voice (docs/plans/journal-voices.md).
// The fight is told without words, so the pages never say what the Seraph is or why; the heroes only say what they saw: the hooded figure risen on three pairs of ash-black wings edged in gold, a broken ring of light over a court with no roof, snow drifting upward, frost pillars with a gold heart.
// The idea every page carries: the hands are still the tell; the farthest hero is where a shard lands and becomes a pillar; a pillar is cover from the light and the blade breaks it; so keep pillars out of blade lines, and not too many standing at the end.
// Move keys are cast names (the journal fires on the cast bar's name). The follow-ups (Return, Afterglow, Ash Landing, Absolution, Weighing, Burial, Hollow Echo, Frost Shadow) have no page of their own.
(window.JOURNAL_DATA = window.JOURNAL_DATA || {}).seraph = {
  // the first time this hero meets it (after the first pull)
  meet: {
    bastion: "The same hooded figure, now hovering on three pairs of ash-black wings edged in gold under a broken ring of light. The roof was gone, and snow drifted upward. Pieces of the ring land where the farthest of us stands and rise as pillars.",
    gloomsworn: "The same hooded one, risen. Three pairs of ash-black wings edged in gold, a broken ring of light, and a court with no roof. The snow fell upward; I have seen skies like that from underneath. The ring drops a piece on the farthest of us, and it becomes a pillar.",
    thresher: "Oh, he has wings now, dear: three pairs, ash-black and edged in gold, and a broken ring of light where the roof used to be. The snow drifts upward, which I find charming. Pieces of the ring land by whoever stands farthest and grow into frosty pillars.",
    bloodreaver: "Wings! Three pairs, black as ash and edged in gold, and the big one hangs under a broken ring of light with the roof torn off and the snow going up! It flings bits of the ring at the farthest of us, and they stand up as ice pillars.",
    runeguard: "The same figure, risen: three pairs of ash-black wings edged in gold, a broken ring of light, and a court without a roof, the snow rising. Recorded: a shard falls on the farthest of us and stands as a pillar, and a pillar throws shade from the light.",
    gorgemaw: "My host has changed the menu and the ceiling: the roof is gone, the snow drifts upward, and three pairs of ash-black wings edged in gold hold him above the floor under a broken ring of light. Shards of it are served to the farthest guest and set as pillars.",
    oathbroker: "The counterparty has been revised: three pairs of ash-black wings edged in gold, a broken ring of light overhead, no roof, the snow rising. A shard of the ring is delivered to the farthest of us and stands as a pillar, to the benefit of whoever shelters behind it.",
    ironpalm: "The same silence, but with wings: three pairs, ash-black, edged in gold, and a broken ring of light over a court with no roof. Snow rose past us. The ring gives a piece to the farthest of us, and a pillar grows there. I watched the hands.",
    ranger: "Hovering now. Three pairs of ash-black wings, gold edges, a broken ring of light above, no roof, snow going up. The beast throws a shard at whoever stands farthest out, and a frost pillar stands where it lands. Cover, if it is put in the right place.",
    shadowblade: "The mark learned to fly, and rudely. Three pairs of ash-black wings edged in gold, a broken ring of light over the court, no roof, snow drifting upward. Each shard of the ring falls on the farthest of us and stands up as a pillar. Shade, at last.",
    pyromancer: "Wings! Three pairs, ash-black and edged in gold, under a broken ring of light that is almost as bright as I am! The roof is gone, the snow drifts upward, and the farthest of us is handed a shard, which stands up as a frost pillar. Shade for the sulking.",
    thermist: "Cold: three pairs of ash-black wings edged in gold, a broken ring of light, no roof, snow rising. Then hot, all at once: it threw a shard at the farthest of us, and a frost pillar stood where it landed. Steady. Cover, if I placed it well.",
    driftblade: "A great bird now, three pairs of ash-black wings edged in gold, hanging under a broken ring of light with no roof and the snow going up, and every shard came down on whoever was farthest out and stood up as a pillar, so I learned which edge to run to.",
    alembist: "Specimen: the same hooded figure, now hovering. Observed: three pairs of ash-black wings edged in gold, a broken ring of light, no roof, snow rising. Note: each shard of the ring lands on the farthest of us and sets as a frost pillar. Label: cover, to be handled with care.",
    threadweaver: "It has grown wings, three pairs of ash-black ones edged in gold, and a broken ring of light hangs over the court like a seam come undone. No roof, and the snow drifts upward. A piece of the ring drops by whoever stands farthest and becomes a frost pillar.",
    marionettist: "A new act: the star hangs above the stage on three pairs of ash-black wings edged in gold, a broken ring of light for a chandelier, the roof struck and the snow drifting up into the flies. Each shard falls by the farthest player and stands as a pillar. (Scenery, supplied by the company.)",
    cleric: "Poor soul, it has wings now: three pairs, ash-black and edged in gold, and a broken ring of light over the court where the roof was. The snow drifted upward. A shard of the ring falls beside whoever stands farthest and rises as a frost pillar. Shelter, of a kind.",
    grovekeeper: "A different sky: no roof, ash cloud, snow drifting upward, and over us three pairs of ash-black wings edged in gold under a broken ring of light. The ring sheds a piece on the farthest of us, and a pillar grows where it lands. Shade, if I tend it right.",
    chronomancer: "It has wings now, which I did not remember until I saw them: three pairs, ash-black, edged in gold, under a broken ring of light and a roofless sky with snow rising. A shard lands by the farthest of us, and a pillar stands there. I will have seen this before.",
    tidecaller: "The roof was gone and the snow rose like spray going the wrong way. The hooded one hung there on three pairs of ash-black wings edged in gold, under a broken ring of light. A shard falls by the farthest of us and a pillar of frost rises, like a rock in the shallows.",
    lanternkeeper: "No roof any more, only an ash sky, and snow drifting upward. It hung above us on three pairs of ash-black wings edged in gold, under a broken ring of light. A piece of the ring fell by the farthest of us and stood up as a pillar with a gold glow in its heart.",
    kenseier: "The same figure, lifted: three pairs of ash-black wings edged in gold, a broken ring of light, no roof, snow rising. Its shards fall on the farthest of us and stand as pillars. A blade's line breaks them; the light cannot pass them. I counted that first.",
    houndmaster: "Big lad's got wings now: three pairs, ash-black, edged in gold, and a broken ring of light over a court with no roof, snow drifting up. Chucks a shard at whoever's farthest out and a pillar stands where it lands. Both dogs wanted to go and sniff it.",
  },
  // after the kill: the wings fold and it lies down in the snow
  win: {
    bastion: "The wings folded, one pair after the next, and the Seraph lay down in the snow. The ring of light went dark above us. The pillars stood where we had put them, and I had never been so glad of a wall.",
    gloomsworn: "The wings closed over it, one pair at a time, and it lay down in the snow like a man going to sleep. I have lain like that. The ring over the court went dark.",
    thresher: "Oh, he folded his wings so neatly, dear, pair after pair, and lay down in the snow as if for a nap. The ring of light went out. I hummed a little, for the quiet.",
    bloodreaver: "Its wings folded, one pair and then the next, and the big one lay down in the snow, still and fine. The ring of light went out over us. I lay down too, in the cold, and laughed until it hurt.",
    runeguard: "The three pairs of wings closed in order; the Seraph lay down in the snow; the ring of light went dark above the court. Every pillar was accounted for, standing or broken. The record is complete.",
    gorgemaw: "The last course went out: wings folded, pair by pair, and my host settled in the snow with the ring of light dark over his head. The pillars melted slowly, like ice in a good cellar. I could eat again.",
    oathbroker: "The wings were furled, pair by pair, and the Seraph lay down in the snow; the ring of light lapsed. Every pillar we raised stood to the last, or was lawfully broken. The matter is closed.",
    ironpalm: "The wings folded. The Seraph lay in the snow, and the ring above us went dark. The snow kept rising for a while, quietly. Then it stopped, and the court was still.",
    ranger: "Wings folded. It went down in the snow and stayed there. Ring overhead gone dark. Snow still drifting up, slower. No more tracks to read.",
    shadowblade: "Its wings folded, one pair after the next, and it lay down in the snow without a glance at any of us. The ring of light went dark. I was the last to leave the court, and no one watched me go.",
    pyromancer: "Down it went, wings folded pair by pair, into the snow, and the ring of light went out over it like the end of a very grand show! I applauded alone. Someone had to.",
    thermist: "Wings folded, one pair, then the next. It lay down in the snow. The ring of light went dark, and the cold in the court let go of me at last, a long slow thaw.",
    driftblade: "It folded its wings pair by pair and sank into the snow, and I ran a slow lap round the court, past every pillar left and every one broken, just to feel the wind come down from the open sky.",
    alembist: "Specimen: at rest. Observed: three pairs of wings folded, the ring of light dark, the Seraph lying in the snow. Note: the pillars were the best reagent we ever made, and the cheapest. Label it and shelve it.",
    threadweaver: "The wings folded, pair by pair, like cloth being put away, and the Seraph lay down in the snow. The ring of light went dark. Every seam we sewed that night held, even the ugly ones.",
    marionettist: "(The wings fold, pair by pair. The star lies down in the snow. The ring of light goes dark above the stage.) The company bowed to the pillars, which had played their part better than I had.",
    cleric: "The wings folded, one pair at a time, and the poor soul lay down in the snow. The ring of light went dark. I knelt by it a moment, and the snow stopped rising.",
    grovekeeper: "It folded its wings, pair by pair, and lay down in the snow, and the ring over the court went dark. The snow stopped climbing and began, at last, to fall. A sky that remembers which way is down.",
    chronomancer: "Wings folded, one pair, then the next, and it lay down in the snow. The ring of light went dark. Nothing needed undoing, and I counted that as the fight's best moment, which I will have said before.",
    tidecaller: "The wings closed over it, pair on pair, like a slow wave settling, and it lay down in the snow. The ring of light went dark. The snow turned about and fell like rain. It was over.",
    lanternkeeper: "The wings folded, one pair at a time, and it lay down in the snow. The ring of light went dark over the court. Every pillar still glowed at its heart for a while after. I let them.",
    kenseier: "The wings folded, pair by pair, and the Seraph lay down in the snow, the ring of light dark above it. Its last stroke came on the beat, and so did the rest. I sheathed the blade.",
    houndmaster: "Big lad folded his wings and lay down in the snow, and the light overhead went out. Both dogs sat by the nearest pillar and watched him a good while. Quiet after. We'll have him down by supper, I told them, and it was true.",
  },
  moves: {
    // ------------------------------------------------------------------- the plain moves (a hand above the floor, wings stirring)
    'Hollow Step': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "It slid across the floor a hand above the stones and swung twice at whoever stood nearest. I made sure that was me, a pace in front of the line. The swings were light.",
      gloomsworn: "It drifted toward the nearest of us and swung twice, wings barely stirring. I made myself the nearest. Two light blows; I was dead for worse.",
      thresher: "Such a polite glide, dear, a hand above the floor, straight to whoever stands closest, and two little swings. So I made sure the closest was someone sturdy, and stayed a pace behind.",
      bloodreaver: "It floated up to the nearest of us and swung twice. Light ones, a tickle! I made sure the nearest was me, and answered every swing, because a friend who floats should still be hit.",
      runeguard: "The sign: it glides toward whoever is nearest and no one else, wings low. The remedy is to be that person if you carry the shield, and let the others keep their distance; the two swings that follow are slight.",
      gorgemaw: "A light appetiser: it drifted to the nearest guest and swung twice. I made sure I was nearest, and took both swings like two bread rolls before the main business.",
      oathbroker: "The Seraph undertakes to attend whoever stands nearest and to swing twice. I stood nearest by design, so the obligation fell to the party best able to meet it, and was met.",
      ironpalm: "It glided to the one nearest and spoke twice, lightly. That was me. I let each swing land, and did not reply in kind. It was only a greeting.",
      ranger: "Glided to whoever stood closest. Two swings. Kept the shield between us and stayed back. Nothing to it.",
      shadowblade: "It wafted toward the nearest of us, as if it had some manners, and swung twice. I made sure the nearest was our shield and not me. Rude of it to hover, though.",
      pyromancer: "It floated at the nearest of us and swung twice, quite politely for a thing with that many wings. I made sure the nearest wasn't me, and went on casting, which was the point.",
      thermist: "Cold and plain: it glides to the nearest of us and swings twice. Light. I stayed far behind the shield and let the nearest be sturdy. A small warm sting for whoever it is.",
      driftblade: "It drifted to the nearest, a hand above the floor, and swung twice, and I was never the nearest, because I never stood anywhere long enough to be, and went round behind while the shield took it.",
      alembist: "Observed: it glides to the nearest and swings twice, wings stirring. Note: keep our shield nearest and the fragile apparatus, myself included, a few paces behind.",
      threadweaver: "It slid up to whoever stood nearest and swung twice. Light work. I kept the shield a pace ahead of the rest so the nearest was never one of my fragile ones, and the thread stayed easy.",
      marionettist: "(Enter the star, a hand above the boards, to the nearest player.) Two swings, small ones. I kept the Doll in the wings and the shield downstage, which is where the star looks first.",
      cleric: "It drifted to the nearest of us and swung twice, not hard. I was glad it was our knight, who stood closest on purpose. A little mending after, and no one the worse.",
      grovekeeper: "It came on like a slow breeze, a hand above the ground, to the nearest of us, and swung twice. Light weather. I kept the sturdy one nearest and the saplings behind.",
      chronomancer: "It glides to whoever is nearest and swings twice, and it did so before I could say it would. Keep the sturdy one nearest. The second swing is only an echo of the first.",
      tidecaller: "Small swells, two of them, on whoever stood nearest, the winged one gliding up in no hurry at all. I kept the water high under our shield, who was nearest on purpose, and the swings broke on him.",
      lanternkeeper: "It glided to the nearest of us and swung twice, a hand above the floor. I hung one light on whoever stood closest, and made sure that was our shield. One light, one swing each.",
      kenseier: "It drifts to the nearest and strikes twice, a beat apart. I stood nearest and met each stroke with the blade as it landed. A light, honest pair, and a good place to warm up.",
      houndmaster: "Floats up to whoever's closest and swings twice. Sent the shield-man in front and held the lads back behind him. Light stuff. Sit.",
    } },
    'Cold Breath': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "A cone of cold breath, aimed at the nearest. I took it square, since it was small, and the others stood out of the cone's width. Frost, but no ice on me. Nothing to hold against.",
      gloomsworn: "It breathed on the nearest of us: a short cone, drawn on the floor. I was the nearest. The cold went in and out. I have been colder in worse company.",
      thresher: "A little cone of frost for the nearest, dear, drawn on the floor first like a polite invitation. I stepped out of it, humming. The snow drifted upward through the gap.",
      bloodreaver: "It blew frost at the nearest of us, a short cone, and I let it have me. A nip! It left no ice, only a bite. The rest stayed out of the cone and kept swinging.",
      runeguard: "The sign: the hood tilts toward the nearest, and a short cone of cold is drawn on the floor. The one it faces stands aside or takes the small share; the others keep out of the cone's width.",
      gorgemaw: "A chilled sorbet, served to the nearest guest in a short cone. It was small and it did not freeze, so I took it myself, and the rest stood out of the dish.",
      oathbroker: "The Seraph tendered a short cone of frost to the nearest party. The sum was small, with no encumbrance. I accepted it in person, and the others kept clear of the cone's width.",
      ironpalm: "A breath, aimed at the nearest, and the nearest was I. It was a cold phrase, short, and it did not freeze me. The others stood out of the cone and let it pass.",
      ranger: "Cone of cold at the nearest, drawn first. Stepped out of the arc, left it to the shield. Small. No ice in it.",
      shadowblade: "The mark breathed on the nearest of us. A short cone, drawn first, which is almost polite. I wasn't nearest, so it only chilled the air where I might have stood.",
      pyromancer: "It breathed frost at the nearest of us, a sulky little cone of cold in the middle of my best spell! I was not the nearest. The knight took it, and I took the credit for standing elsewhere.",
      thermist: "A short cone of frost at the nearest. Cold, but small. I stood out of the cone's width, and then hot with relief, swung in again behind the one who took it. No ice came of it.",
      driftblade: "Frost came out of the hood in a short cone aimed at the nearest of us, and I was never nearest, I was already round the side and through the snow, and it breathed on a shield instead.",
      alembist: "Observed: a short cone of frost at the nearest, drawn on the floor before it comes. Note: small, no freezing. Whoever is nearest takes it; the rest stand outside the cone's width.",
      threadweaver: "A short cone of frost at the nearest one, drawn plain on the floor. Not a snag, just a nick. I let the nearest take it and kept the rest of my stitches outside the cone.",
      marionettist: "(A cone of frost, drawn on the boards for the nearest player. Small, no ice.) The shield took it. The company stepped out of the cone's width and did not miss the cue.",
      cleric: "It breathed on whoever was nearest, a short cone of frost, drawn on the floor first. Small and no ice to it, so I mended after rather than before, and the rest kept off the cone. A gentle one.",
      grovekeeper: "A short breath of frost for the nearest, drawn on the ground before it came, like the first cold morning. Small, no ice in it. The nearest took it and the rest stood wide.",
      chronomancer: "The cone is drawn, then the breath follows it, always in that order. It aims at the nearest, small, no ice. I stepped out one beat early, or stood in it with a shield; either way it was done.",
      tidecaller: "A small cold swell, rolling out in a short cone at the nearest of us. It left no ice behind. Our shield stood in it and it ebbed away, and the rest of us were already out of its width.",
      lanternkeeper: "A short cone of frost, drawn on the floor for the nearest of us. I lit the floor beside the cone, a lamp for the others to stand at, outside it. Small, with no ice.",
      kenseier: "A short breath, aimed at the nearest. The cone was drawn beforehand, which is courtesy. A blade does not turn a breath, so I stood in it and let it pass, and the others stood out.",
      houndmaster: "Frost in a short cone at the nearest. Whistled the lads wide of it, took it myself, no ice on me. Mild stuff.",
    } },
    'Frostfall': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "Three circles of frost drawn under the three farthest of us, and I was not one, for once. Whoever stood in one stepped out. The snow came down in them for a moment, against the drift.",
      gloomsworn: "Three circles drawn on the floor beneath the farthest of us. I was near enough to be left out. Each of them stepped out of their own and nothing came of it. The snow had changed its mind about up.",
      thresher: "Three little circles for the three farthest, dear, drawn on the floor with such good manners. We each stepped out of ours and the frost came down on empty snow.",
      bloodreaver: "Frost rained into three circles under the farthest of us. I was too close to get one, a shame. The others stepped aside and it fell on bare floor, which seemed a waste of a good bruise.",
      runeguard: "The sign: three circles on the floor beneath the three farthest of us. The remedy: each moves out of their own, and none is hurt. Distance, I noted, is exactly what it looks for.",
      gorgemaw: "Three small helpings of frost, set down on the three farthest plates. I was too near the kitchen to be served. Those who were served stepped off their plates, and the helpings landed on bare stone.",
      oathbroker: "Three modest levies, assessed against the three farthest of us. Each party stood out of the circle drawn for it, and the levy lapsed unpaid. The nearest were exempt, and I counted myself fortunate.",
      ironpalm: "Three circles, on the three farthest. They spoke to those who stood alone. Each stepped aside, and the frost fell on empty floor. Distance is no hiding place.",
      ranger: "Three circles, drawn on the three farthest. I was one. Stepped out, drew, stepped out again. The snow went up through the frost that fell.",
      shadowblade: "The mark singled out the three of us standing farthest from it, each of us ringed in frost. Being far away doesn't make you forgotten. I stepped out of mine, in the dark, with my usual grace.",
      pyromancer: "Three circles of frost on the three farthest, and I was one, because I like some room! I stepped out with great dignity and finished the spell from the edge of the circle. Bright, and a little cold.",
      thermist: "Three circles on the farthest three. Cold: step out. I was one of them, and ran hot with surprise, and stepped aside to the next patch of floor. The frost fell where I had been.",
      driftblade: "Frost came down in three circles on the three farthest of us and I was one of them, naturally, so I slipped out of mine and round and through the snow, and it fell on bare ground behind me.",
      alembist: "Observed: three circles of frost on the three of us farthest from the Seraph. Note: light, and plainly drawn, so stepping out suffices. Those near it are overlooked; keep that in mind for the shards.",
      threadweaver: "Three circles on the three farthest, so the strands pulling hardest. Each of us stepped out of our own and it came down on bare floor. A neat hem for once, and I did not need to mend.",
      marionettist: "(Three spotlights of frost, upon the three players farthest from the star.) Each stepped out of their light on cue. I took the Doll off the mark first; she dislikes being spotlit.",
      cleric: "Frost fell in three circles on the three farthest of us. I called them out gently and each stepped aside, and it landed on empty snow. No mending needed, which is the best sort.",
      grovekeeper: "Three patches of frost came down on the three farthest of us, small and drawn first, like a sudden hail. We each stepped out of our own. The rest of the sky went on snowing upward.",
      chronomancer: "It names the three farthest and then the frost arrives. I stepped out as it named me, which is the only way to get there before it does, and I did not mind. The snow still went up.",
      tidecaller: "Three small squalls, falling on the three of us farthest out. Each stepped out of our own and it broke on empty floor. The far shore is not safer, only slower to be reached.",
      lanternkeeper: "Three circles of frost, on the three farthest from the light. Three lights, four of us, and I stepped out of mine. It fell on bare floor, and the snow drifted up past it.",
      kenseier: "Three circles under the three farthest. No beat to count, only the drawing. I stepped aside as it fell and the others did the same. The frost struck bare stone.",
      houndmaster: "Frost in three circles under the three farthest. I was one, with a dog at each knee. Whistled the lads out of it and stepped after. Landed on bare floor.",
    } },
    'Wingbeat': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "The wings swept and threw us all toward the walls. I picked my ground first, so there was open floor behind me. A pillar behind you stops you hard. Footing mattered more than the shield.",
      gloomsworn: "The wings beat once and every one of us went flying outward. I made sure no pillar stood behind me, because I know what stopping hard feels like. Wide, open floor is kinder.",
      thresher: "A great wingbeat, dear, and off we all flew, away from him like leaves. I checked beforehand that no pillar stood behind me, because they stop you rather abruptly.",
      bloodreaver: "One beat of those wings and we all flew out like thrown knives! I picked a spot with nothing solid behind me. A pillar stops you hard, and I'd rather choose my own bruises.",
      runeguard: "The wings beat once and flung all of us from it toward the walls. Mark the line behind you: a pillar in it stops you short and hard, so stand where the way outward lies open.",
      gorgemaw: "The wings cleared the table in one sweep: every guest sent toward the walls. I made sure there was nothing but floor behind me. A pillar is a hard thing to be served against.",
      oathbroker: "The Seraph's wingbeat displaces all parties outward, toward the walls. A pillar in the path arrests one forcibly and at cost. I therefore stood where the path behind me was clear, as a matter of prudence.",
      ironpalm: "The wings spoke once and we were thrown outward. I looked behind me first. A pillar there would have answered harder than the wall. I chose open floor and let myself fly.",
      ranger: "Wings beat, everyone thrown out toward the wall. Checked my back first: no pillar in the line. A pillar stops you hard. Landed on my feet.",
      shadowblade: "It flapped, rudely, and threw us all toward the walls. A pillar behind you stops you very suddenly, so I made sure I had only open floor at my back before it began.",
      pyromancer: "It beat its wings and I was flung toward the wall in the middle of a spell! Lesson: nothing solid at your back, because a pillar stops you with great discourtesy. I flew out cleanly and finished from the far side.",
      thermist: "One beat of the wings: cold, wide, everyone thrown outward. I had checked the floor behind me, and found it open. A pillar there stops you hard. Then I swung back in, warm again.",
      driftblade: "The wings beat and we all went flying toward the walls, which I enjoyed, being thrown is just a long step, but I picked a line with no pillar in it first, because a pillar stops you cold.",
      alembist: "Observed: one wingbeat, and all of us thrown outward toward the walls. Note: a pillar behind you stops you hard, so I checked behind me for open floor. The reagents stayed in their bottles.",
      threadweaver: "The wings beat and all of us were pulled outward like loose threads. Mind what's behind you: a pillar stops you hard, and I told my stitches to stand where the way out was clear.",
      marionettist: "(The star beats his wings, and the company is flung to the wings of the stage.) I checked behind me first: a pillar upstage stops a player very hard. The Doll, ever sensible, stood with open boards behind her.",
      cleric: "One great beat of the wings threw every one of us outward. I asked my friends to stand with open floor behind them, because a pillar stops you hard, and no one wants a bruise from their own shelter.",
      grovekeeper: "The wingbeat came like a gust and threw us toward the walls. I had planted myself where nothing stood behind me. A pillar will stop a body hard, and I'd rather lean on a tree.",
      chronomancer: "The wings beat once and everyone flew outward; I had already looked behind me, which is the nicest part of knowing what's coming. A pillar stops you hard. Open floor, always.",
      tidecaller: "The wings gave one great push, like a wave going out, and all of us were carried toward the walls. I kept clear floor behind me. A pillar is a rock, and moving water stops hard on a rock.",
      lanternkeeper: "One beat of the wings and all of us were thrown toward the walls. I stood where nothing was behind me but floor. A pillar stops you hard, and I don't light a lamp for that.",
      kenseier: "The wings beat once and threw us outward. There is no blade for it. I chose open floor behind me, because a pillar stops a body short and hard, and a wall less so. Then I walked back.",
      houndmaster: "Wing-beat threw the lot of us toward the walls, dogs too. Whistled the lads in close first, so nothing solid stood behind any of us. A pillar stops you hard.",
    } },
    // ------------------------------------------------------------------- the halo, the blade and the light
    'Broken Halo': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "A piece of the ring tore loose and fell on the farthest of us. The circle was drawn first. We stepped off it, and a pillar stood where it had been. Whoever goes far chooses where the cover will be.",
      gloomsworn: "A shard of the ring came down on the farthest of us, the circle drawn on the floor beforehand. The one furthest out stepped off, and a pillar of frost stood in their place. Cover, if you are far away on purpose.",
      thresher: "Whoever stands farthest gets a gift from the sky, dear: a shard of the ring, the circle drawn first. Step off it, and a frosty pillar stands where you were. Choose who goes far, and where.",
      bloodreaver: "It tore a piece off the ring and flung it at whoever stood farthest out! The circle shows first. Step off, it hits the floor, and a pillar of ice stands there. I wanted to be hit by it, but the pillar was worth more.",
      runeguard: "A shard drawn from the ring falls on the farthest of us; the circle is shown beforehand. Step off before it lands, and a frost pillar rises on the spot. The placement of every pillar is therefore chosen by who walks farthest.",
      gorgemaw: "My host tore a crust off his ring and threw it at the farthest guest. The circle on the floor showed it coming. The guest stepped aside, and the crust set into a pillar of frost where it fell.",
      oathbroker: "A shard is delivered to whichever party stands farthest, the address drawn beforehand as a circle. The recipient declines by stepping out of it, and a pillar is established upon the spot. We choose the address.",
      ironpalm: "A piece of the ring fell toward the farthest of us. The circle came first. The one it called stepped out, and it landed, and a pillar of frost stood in the quiet. Where you stand far is where you ask for cover.",
      ranger: "Shard thrown at the farthest. Circle drawn first. Stepped out, and a pillar stood where I'd been. Walked to the spot I wanted cover and stood there. Simple.",
      shadowblade: "The mark threw a piece of its halo at the farthest of us, and the circle was drawn first, politely. I stepped out and a frost pillar rose in the very place I'd been. A hiding place, made to order.",
      pyromancer: "A shard fell from the ring onto the farthest of us, and I may have made sure that was me, standing off at the best distance for cover! The circle was drawn first. I stepped aside and a pillar rose. Magnificent, and practical.",
      thermist: "Cold: a shard drops on the farthest of us, circle drawn first. Step out. Hot: it hit the floor, and a frost pillar stood up there, gold in its heart. Where I stood far was where the cover rose.",
      driftblade: "It threw a shard of the ring at whoever was farthest, the circle drawn first on the floor, so I ran to the place I wanted a pillar and stood a breath and slipped through the edge as it landed.",
      alembist: "Observed: a shard from the ring, aimed at the farthest of us, the circle drawn first. Note: step out before it lands. A frost pillar sets where it fell, so the farthest decides where our cover is.",
      threadweaver: "A shard dropped on the farthest of us, the circle drawn plainly first. I told whoever it was to step off, and a frost pillar stood in the spot. Cover goes where the farthest one chooses to stand.",
      marionettist: "(A shard of the halo falls upon the player farthest from the star; the spot is lit first.) The player steps out, and a frost pillar takes the mark. The farthest player sets the scenery.",
      cleric: "A shard of the ring fell on the farthest of us, the circle drawn first. I asked that one to step out in good time, and a frost pillar stood there. We chose who would stand far, to put it where it was wanted.",
      grovekeeper: "A shard came down on the farthest of us, the circle drawn on the ground first. Step off it, and a pillar of frost takes root where it fell. I thought of where I wanted the shade, and who should stand there.",
      chronomancer: "The shard is thrown at the farthest, the circle drawn, then it lands. I stepped out on the drawing, so I was gone before it came, and a pillar stood in my old place. Cover is simply arriving where you need it.",
      tidecaller: "A shard fell toward the farthest of us, the circle drawn first. Whoever stood there stepped aside and it struck bare floor. A pillar of frost rose, like a rock left where the water recedes.",
      lanternkeeper: "A piece of the ring fell on the farthest of us. The circle came first, so we stepped out. A pillar stood in the lit spot, gold at its heart. One more light that doesn't burn out.",
      kenseier: "A shard is thrown at the farthest, the circle drawn a beat before. I stepped out of the circle at the landing and the frost stood up where it had been. A pillar is a wall one can place.",
      houndmaster: "Piece of the ring flung at whoever's farthest out, circle drawn first. Stepped off it, and a frost pillar stood there. Put the farthest man where we wanted cover and the dogs under it.",
    } },
    'Returning Edge': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "The blade went down a line at one of our strikers, and nothing in front stopped it, not even me. It broke every pillar it crossed and stuck in the wall. Then it came back along a curve, and we stayed off it.",
      gloomsworn: "It threw the blade down a line at one of the strikers. Not even I could stop this one; it went through, shattered a pillar, and froze the one it hit. Then it came back curved. We stood off the curve.",
      thresher: "The blade goes out along a line at one of us, dear, and no shield can catch it, and any pillar in its way breaks. It rests in the wall a moment, then returns by a curve. Keep your pillars off the line.",
      bloodreaver: "A thrown blade at one of the strikers, straight through everything, pillars too! It froze its mark and stuck in the wall. Then it came back on a curve. We moved off the line before and off the curve after.",
      runeguard: "The blade is thrown down a line at one striker and no shield will stop it; it shatters every pillar it passes and freezes the one it finds. Then it returns by a curve, drawn beforehand. Keep pillars off the line and bodies off the curve.",
      gorgemaw: "A skewer thrown at one of the strikers, straight through the whole kitchen: it broke the pillar in its way and froze the poor guest. It buried itself in the wall, then came back round in an arc. I stood clear of the arc.",
      oathbroker: "The blade is delivered to a single striker, and no surety stops it; it shatters any pillar on its line, freezes the recipient, and lodges in the wall. It then returns along a drawn curve. We keep pillars off the line and ourselves off the return.",
      ironpalm: "A long phrase, thrown down a line at one of the strikers. No hand could stop it. It broke the pillar it crossed and froze its mark, then came back on a curve. We kept the line clear, and then the curve.",
      ranger: "Blade thrown down a line at one of the strikers. Nothing stops it, shield included. Breaks any pillar on the line. Buried in the wall, then came back on a curve. Led the line wide of the pillars, stayed off the curve.",
      shadowblade: "It threw its blade at one of us like a rude introduction, and not even our shield could catch it. Pillars on the line broke. It stuck in the wall, then came back round the long way. I took it away from the pillars first.",
      pyromancer: "A blade thrown straight at one of us strikers, through pillars and shields alike! It froze me solid for a moment, a touch dramatic. I'd led the line away from our cover, and stayed off the arc when it came back.",
      thermist: "Cold: the blade runs down a line at one of us and nothing stops it, and any pillar on the line breaks. Hot: the freeze. Then it came back on a curve, and we were already off it.",
      driftblade: "It threw the blade straight down a line at one of us, through pillars and shields, so I took the line wide of every pillar and through the open side, and when the blade swung back in a curve I was already round it.",
      alembist: "Observed: a blade thrown down a line at a striker; it shatters pillars and cannot be stopped, even by a shield. Note: frost on whoever it finds, and a curve drawn back from the wall. Label the line, keep pillars off it.",
      threadweaver: "The blade ran down a line at one of the strikers and nothing could catch it, the pillars it crossed snapped like thread. I got the frost off the one it found, and we kept off the curved line it came back by.",
      marionettist: "(The blade is thrown at a player; nothing in the scene can stop it, and any pillar upon the line shatters.) It freezes its mark and returns in a curve. I walked the line clear of the scenery first.",
      cleric: "The blade was thrown at one of our strikers, and nothing could stand in its way. It broke the pillar it crossed and left the poor soul frozen. When it came back on a curve, we were off it. I mended the frost after.",
      grovekeeper: "A thrown blade, straight as a frost line at one of the strikers, and it broke every pillar it crossed. It stuck in the wall, then swung back in a curve. I kept the pillars out of its line and my lot out of its curve.",
      chronomancer: "The blade goes out at a striker, and nothing stops it; it breaks any pillar it meets, then lodges in the wall and comes back by a curve. I stepped off the curve before it started. Pillars off the line, always.",
      tidecaller: "The blade ran out like an outgoing wave at one of the strikers, breaking every pillar it crossed, and it came back by a long curve, as water does. A shield could not stop it. We kept pillars off its line.",
      lanternkeeper: "The blade went down a line at one of the strikers and no shield could stop it. It shattered any pillar on the line. I set the lamp I'd lit for them away from the line, and we kept off the curve it came back by.",
      kenseier: "A thrown blade at one of the strikers, down a line. I cannot meet it; it passes through the shield and breaks every pillar on its way. It buries itself, then returns by a curve. The line is the lesson.",
      houndmaster: "Blade thrown at one of the strikers, clean through the shield-man, and any pillar in its way broke. Buried in the wall, then came back round on a curve. Kept the line off our cover and the lads off the curve.",
    } },
    'Radiance': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "The healer glowed, and six rays stood out of the glow. A pillar between a body and that light stops the ray. We ran behind the nearest pillar, with the healer on the open side, and the last burst fell only round the healer's feet.",
      gloomsworn: "The healer lit up and rays came out in all six directions. A pillar in the way stops them. I stood behind one, with the light on the other side of it. A dead man learns to value a wall.",
      thresher: "Our healer lit up like a lantern, dear, and six rays reached out. A pillar between you and that glow is a very good umbrella, so we tucked in behind one while the healer stood in the open. The burst at their feet was theirs alone.",
      bloodreaver: "Six rays shot out of the healer! I wanted to stand in one and see. But a pillar stops them, so I got behind one like everyone else, and stayed clear of the burst the glow ended with.",
      runeguard: "The sign: the healer glows, and six rays are drawn from them at even angles. A pillar between a body and that glow stops the ray. We took our places behind it, and stood off from the healer for the burst that ends it.",
      gorgemaw: "Six skewers of light from the healer's glow, and a pillar is a very fine plate to hide behind. I stood behind one with the others, away from the final burst round the healer's feet.",
      oathbroker: "Six rays issue from the healer, each binding on whoever it crosses unless a pillar intervenes. We placed ourselves behind the pillar, out of the healer's sight, and kept clear of the burst that closes the matter.",
      ironpalm: "The healer glowed and six rays leaned out of the glow. A pillar answers a ray. I stood behind it, out of the healer's sight, with the others, and stayed clear of the last burst. We did not speak.",
      ranger: "Six rays out of the healer. Pillar stops a ray. Stood behind one, healer on the far side, out of the line. Kept clear of the burst at the end.",
      shadowblade: "The healer lit up, and six rays reached out, which is how the light hunts. A pillar blocks the line between us. I stood in its shadow, which is where I like to be, and watched the burst from outside.",
      pyromancer: "The healer blazed and sent out six rays! A rival, almost. A pillar stops a ray, so I stood behind one and sulked at the unfairness of being shaded. Out of the burst's reach, too, thank you.",
      thermist: "Hot: six rays out of the healer's glow. Cold: a pillar between you and the glow stops the ray. I stood behind one, out of sight of the healer, and stayed clear of the burst. Steady.",
      driftblade: "Six rays swept out of the healer and I slid round to the back of a pillar and stayed there, out of the glow's sight, and then away from the burst round the healer when the rays died. A short, tidy hide.",
      alembist: "Observed: I glowed, and six rays came out of me. Note: a pillar between my light and a friend stops the ray, so they stood behind it. I stood in the open. The burst at the end was mine, and I'd made it.",
      threadweaver: "Six rays pulled out of me, taut as thread. A pillar cuts the ray, so I put the rest behind one, myself in front of it, and let the final burst fall round my own feet.",
      marionettist: "(Six spotlights from the healer.) A pillar upstage blocks a spotlight, so the company took their places behind it, out of the healer's view, and left the healer centre stage for the final burst.",
      cleric: "The light opened in me, and six rays reached out. A pillar between a friend and me stops the ray, so they stood behind one while I stayed in the open. The burst at my own feet was mine to bear, and I did.",
      grovekeeper: "Six rays came out of me like roots from a seed, and a pillar stops a root. My lot stood behind one, out of my sight. I stood out in the open, and the burst at my feet came after, and I was ready for it.",
      chronomancer: "I glowed, six rays went out, and I stepped to the open side of a pillar one beat early, so the rest could stand behind it. The burst round my feet came last. I had a plan for that, which I will have had.",
      tidecaller: "The glow rose in me slowly, and six rays went out. I stood on the open side of a pillar and the others in its shadow, where the light cannot reach. The final burst broke round my feet alone.",
      lanternkeeper: "My lamp lit and six rays went out of it. A pillar between my light and a friend stops the ray, so I lit the open side and they stood behind. One pillar, three of them. The last burst was only round my feet.",
      kenseier: "Six rays out of the healer. A blade does not turn light, so I put stone in front of it: a pillar between me and the glow. We stood behind it, and stayed clear of the burst that ended it.",
      houndmaster: "Six rays off the healer, lit up like a lamp. Pillar stops a ray. Got the pair and myself behind one, out of the healer's sight, and clear of the burst at the end. Sit.",
    } },
    'Wingfall': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "It rose and dove three times: a line at each striker, then the healer. I took the first dive on my shield. The rest read their lines and left them. Pillars in the dives were shattered, and we kept out of the landing circle.",
      gloomsworn: "It rose and came down three times along drawn lines. I stood in the first line and took it whole. The pillars in the way broke, so I trusted none of them. At the end, we left the landing circle to the snow.",
      thresher: "Up it went, dear, and down three times, each along a drawn line, and every pillar in the way was broken. I stood well off the lines and out of the last landing, and our shield stood in the first, which is manners.",
      bloodreaver: "Up it went, and down three times along lines like scars! I stood in the first and took the blow on my chest, glorious. The pillars in the lines broke, and we all stood clear of the landing at the end.",
      runeguard: "The sign: it rises. Three dives follow, each along a drawn line: the first at a striker, which the shield takes by standing in it; the others, we step from. Any pillar in a line is shattered; the landing at the end is a circle to leave.",
      gorgemaw: "The host rose and served three dives down three drawn lines. I stood in the first and ate it. Every pillar in a line was broken like a plate. We kept out of the last landing.",
      oathbroker: "Three dives are issued along drawn lines. I placed myself in the first as surety, and it stopped upon me. The other lines each party left in good time. Any pillar on a line is forfeit, and the landing circle is to be vacated.",
      ironpalm: "It rose, then fell three times along the lines it had drawn. I stood in the first and received it. The others stepped out of theirs, and every pillar on a line was broken. Then we left the place it landed.",
      ranger: "Rose out of reach, dove three times along drawn lines. Our shield stood in the first. Moved off the others. Pillars on a line broke. Stayed out of the final landing.",
      shadowblade: "It flew out of reach and came down three times, each down a drawn line, and our shield stood in the first. I walked out of mine. Every pillar in a line was broken, so no hiding there. I stayed clear of the landing.",
      pyromancer: "It rose out of reach in the middle of my best spell, and dove three times down drawn lines! Our shield took the first. I stepped out of mine, and kept away from the pillars in the lines, which broke. Then out of the landing circle.",
      thermist: "Cold: it rises, three dives along drawn lines, our shield in the first. Step out of the others. Pillars in a line break. Hot: the landing circle, and the freeze held me until the end. Stay clear.",
      driftblade: "It rose and came down three times along lines it had drawn, and I was through mine and out the far side before the dive landed, while our shield stood in the first line, and the pillars in the lines broke like ice.",
      alembist: "Observed: it rises out of reach and dives three times along drawn lines. Note: the shield stands in the first; the others step out of theirs. Pillars on a line shatter. The landing circle at the end must be left.",
      threadweaver: "Three dives, each down a drawn line, our shield in the first. The others stepped out of theirs. Any pillar in a line snapped. I mended the frozen ones, and nobody stood in the landing circle.",
      marionettist: "(The star rises into the flies, and dives three times along marked lines.) Our shield took the first. The rest left their marks, and the pillars on the lines broke like scenery. The last landing is a spot to avoid.",
      cleric: "It rose and dove three times along drawn lines. Our knight stood in the first line and took it, and the others stepped from theirs. The pillars on the lines broke, so none of us hid there. I mended the frozen after, outside the landing.",
      grovekeeper: "It rose like a cloud lifting, and came down three times along drawn lines. Our shield stood in the first. Pillars in a line broke, so I sheltered nothing there. I mended the frozen after, well clear of the landing.",
      chronomancer: "Three dives, each along a line drawn beforehand. Our shield steps into the first before it comes. The others step out of theirs. Pillars on the lines shatter. The landing circle comes last; I left it early.",
      tidecaller: "It rose out of reach, a wave drawn back, then broke three times along drawn lines. Our shield took the first. Pillars in the lines went to pieces. I mended the frozen once the landing had passed.",
      lanternkeeper: "It rose and came down three times, each along a drawn line. Our shield stood in the first. The pillars on any line were broken. I put no light in them, and set my lamps well away from where it would land.",
      kenseier: "Three dives, each along a drawn line. The first I met standing in its path, and it stopped on me. The others stepped out. A pillar in a line is broken. The landing is a circle to leave.",
      houndmaster: "Big lad rose and dove three times down drawn lines. Shield-man took the first, the rest of us stepped off ours, dogs too. Pillars in the lines broke. Stayed out of the landing circle.",
    } },
    'Following Light': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "A slow light drifted after the healer, and wherever it passed the floor froze into patches that stayed. The healer led it round the edge of the court, so the middle stayed ours. At the end it flared; we stood clear.",
      gloomsworn: "A slow light followed the healer and left patches of frost on the floor behind it. I did not walk in them. The healer led it round the edge, where nobody needed to stand, and we stayed clear of the flare when it stopped.",
      thresher: "A slow, sweet light followed our healer, dear, and froze the floor behind it into patches. Do walk it round the edge, away from the middle, and the rest of us will stay clear when it flares at the end.",
      bloodreaver: "The slow light followed the healer and froze the ground into patches wherever it went. I stayed out of the patches, which bit! The healer led it round the edge, and I stood clear when it flared.",
      runeguard: "The sign: a light moves slowly after the healer, freezing patches in its wake that remain. The remedy: the healer leads it around the margin of the court, never through the middle, and the rest keep from the patches and from the flare.",
      gorgemaw: "A slow dish of light trailed the healer, leaving frozen puddles on the floor. The healer led it round the rim of the room, and we kept away from the puddles and from the final flare.",
      oathbroker: "A slow light is bound to the healer and leaves frost behind it, which persists. The healer leads it along the edge, leaving the middle unencumbered, and the rest of us avoid the patches and the flare at the end.",
      ironpalm: "A slow light followed the healer, and the floor froze behind it. The healer led it in a long circle round the edge, away from us. I stepped around the patches. At the end the light flared, and we were already clear.",
      ranger: "Slow light followed the healer, frost patches behind it. Healer walked it round the wall. Stayed off the patches, and clear of the flare at the stop.",
      shadowblade: "A slow light crept after the healer and froze the floor in patches. I kept to the places it hadn't touched. The healer led it round the edge, which is manners, and I stayed away when it flared.",
      pyromancer: "A slow light crawled after the healer, freezing patches behind it, and I resented every inch of lost floor! The healer led it round the edge, so the middle stayed mine. It flared and I was already clear.",
      thermist: "Cold: a slow light, trailing the healer, and the patches it froze. The healer walked it wide so the middle stayed free. Hot: the flare when it stopped, and I was already gone.",
      driftblade: "A slow light followed the healer and froze the floor in patches, and the healer led it round the edge in a long loop while I slipped through the gaps and across the middle and was clear when it flared.",
      alembist: "Observed: a slow light follows the healer, leaving frost patches that stay. Note: the healer leads it round the edge, so the patches lie where nobody needs to stand. The flare at the end must be left.",
      threadweaver: "A slow light followed me, trailing frost behind. I led it in a loop round the edge, away from my stitches, so the patches lay along the wall. When it stopped I'd already left, and so had everyone else.",
      marionettist: "(A slow light follows the healer across the stage, freezing the boards in patches.) The healer led it round the edge of the court, the company kept to the middle, and no one stood by the flare at the end.",
      cleric: "A slow light followed me, and the floor froze behind it in patches. I led it round the edge of the court, away from the others, and when it stopped I was already gone. Do mind the frost, my friends.",
      grovekeeper: "A slow light followed me and left frost where it passed, like a late snowfall. I walked it round the edge of the court, away from my lot, so the middle stayed green. It flared where it stopped, and I was not there.",
      chronomancer: "The slow light follows me, leaves patches, and flares where it stops. So I walked it round the edge, early, and left the middle to the others. By the time it stopped, I had moved on. I always have.",
      tidecaller: "A slow light followed me, leaving frost where it passed, as the sea leaves wrack. I led it round the edge of the court, away from the others, and the patches lay along the wall. The flare came on an empty shore.",
      lanternkeeper: "The slow light followed me, so I walked it round the edge of the court, past the pillars, and left it no frost to spoil the middle. The patches lay along the wall. When it flared, it flared at nobody.",
      kenseier: "A slow light followed the healer and froze the floor behind it. No beat to count. The healer led it round the edge, and I stayed out of the patches and away from the flare at the end.",
      houndmaster: "Slow light trailing the healer, frost patches left behind. Healer walked it round the edge, the long way. Kept the lads off the frost, and well clear of it when it flared.",
    } },
    'Benediction': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "A column of light came down on the healer, and then it struck everyone who could see them. I stood behind a pillar with the healer on the far side. A second blow followed along the same sight. The healer could not hide; we kept the healer alive.",
      gloomsworn: "A column of light fell on the healer, and then on everyone with a clear view of the healer. I stood behind a pillar. The healer could not, and bore it. A second blow followed along the same sight, and I stayed put.",
      thresher: "A column of light came down on the healer, dear, and then struck everyone who could see them. Stand behind a pillar, out of sight, and let the healer be healed instead. The second blow follows the same sight.",
      bloodreaver: "A column of light fell on the healer and struck everyone who could see them! I got behind a pillar and the light broke on it. The healer took it in the open, brave, and we patched them up before the second blow.",
      runeguard: "The sign: a column of light descends on the healer. Then it strikes all who have the healer in sight; a second strike follows along the same sightline. We stood behind a pillar. The healer could not, and was mended.",
      gorgemaw: "A column of light came down on the healer, and then a bite for every guest who could see them. I stood behind a pillar, out of sight. The healer was served in the open, twice, and mended between courses.",
      oathbroker: "A column of light is laid on the healer, then charged against every party in the healer's sight, and charged again shortly after. I took the pillar's shelter, as the contract permits. The healer, unsheltered, was made good between charges.",
      ironpalm: "A column fell on the healer, then a blow for everyone who could see them, then a second down the same sight. I stood behind a pillar and was not in sight. The healer could not hide, so we healed the healer.",
      ranger: "Column of light on the healer. Then a hit on everyone with a line of sight to them, and again soon after. Stood behind a pillar from the healer. Healer can't hide; the rest did.",
      shadowblade: "A column of light fell on the healer, and then on everyone who could see them, which is the real trouble. I stood behind a pillar, where I am never seen. The healer, poor thing, had nowhere to be unseen.",
      pyromancer: "A column of light hit the healer, then everyone who could see them, then again! Behind a pillar is the only place to be seen by no one. I sulked there while the healer took it in the open.",
      thermist: "Cold: a column falls on the healer. Then hot, a blow for everyone who can see them. I stood behind a pillar, out of sight, and the second blow missed me. The healer had nowhere to hide; we mended them.",
      driftblade: "A column of light came down on the healer and then everyone in the healer's sight was struck, and again, so I got behind a pillar, round the back and out of sight, and stayed there, while the healer was mended.",
      alembist: "Observed: a column on the healer, then a hit for every hero in the healer's sight, then another along the same sight. Note: stand behind a pillar from the healer. The healer cannot hide; dose the healer.",
      threadweaver: "A column of light dropped on me, and then a blow on everyone who could see me. I put my stitches behind a pillar, out of my sight, and took the second blow in the open. Not neat, but I'd rather mend myself than all of them.",
      marionettist: "(The column falls on the healer; then a blow to anyone in the healer's sight, and another after.) The company took cover behind a pillar, out of the healer's view. The healer takes the scene alone.",
      cleric: "The light came down on me, and then struck everyone who could see me. I asked my friends to stand behind a pillar, out of my sight, and I took the rest myself. Grace is easier to give than to stand in.",
      grovekeeper: "A column of light fell on me, then struck everyone who could see me. My lot stood behind a pillar, out of sight, like seedlings under a stone. I couldn't hide, so I rooted and took it, and healed myself between blows.",
      chronomancer: "A column came down on me, and then a blow struck everyone who could see me, and again a little after. I told them to stand behind a pillar, out of my sight. I could not, so I healed myself on the gap.",
      tidecaller: "The light fell on me from the ring, and struck all who could see me, and again after. The pillar stood between me and the others, and I raised the water in myself for the open blows.",
      lanternkeeper: "A column of light fell on me, and then on everyone who could see me. I made sure there was a pillar between me and each of them. I had no pillar. I mended myself through both blows.",
      kenseier: "A column fell on the healer, and then on all who could see them. A blade cannot turn light, so I put stone between myself and the healer: a pillar. The healer had none. The rest of us kept the healer alive.",
      houndmaster: "Column of light on the healer, then a hit on all that could see them, and again. Got behind a pillar, dogs and all, out of sight. Healer couldn't hide, and mended through it.",
    } },
    'The Scales': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "The floor split into a half of blade and a half of light, and both its hands were open. The strikers belonged in the light, the healer in the blade, and I could stand anywhere. When the halves turned, we crossed again. The blow after fell on all of us.",
      gloomsworn: "The court was cut in two, a blade half and a light half, with the Seraph's hands open over both. The strikers stood in the light, the healer in the blade, and I anywhere. Then the halves turned and we crossed again, round the pillars.",
      thresher: "The floor splits in two, dear, blade side and light side. The dancers stand in the light, our healer in the blade, and the shield wherever. When it turns, we all cross again, and walk round the pillars, please. The last blow comes for everyone.",
      bloodreaver: "The room split in two halves, one of blade and one of light! Strikers in the light half, healer in the blade half, me wherever the fun was. It turned and we crossed again, round the pillars, and the blow after took us all.",
      runeguard: "The sign: both hands open, and the floor halves into blade and light. The strikers go to the light half, the healer to the blade half; the shield may stand anywhere. The halves turn, and all cross again, round the pillars. A last blow follows.",
      gorgemaw: "The table was divided: a blade half and a light half. The strikers sat at the light side, the healer at the blade side, and I wherever the food was. When the halves turned, we crossed again, around the pillars, and then the last blow fell on us all.",
      oathbroker: "The floor is partitioned: a half of blade, a half of light. The strikers belong in the light, the healer in the blade, and I may stand in either. When the halves turn, all parties cross again, round the pillars, and are weighed together.",
      ironpalm: "Two halves, one of blade and one of light. The strikers took the light, the healer the blade. I stood where I liked. Then the halves turned, and we crossed again round the pillars. The last blow fell on all.",
      ranger: "Floor split in two, blade half and light half. Strikers to the light, healer to the blade, shield anywhere. Halves turned, crossed again, round the pillars. Last blow on everyone.",
      shadowblade: "The floor was cut in two, blade and light, and both its hands showed. Strikers belong on the light side, the healer on the blade side, our shield anywhere. It turned, and we slipped across again, round the pillars.",
      pyromancer: "The floor split in two, blade half and light half, and I was NOT going to stand on the wrong one! Strikers to the light, healer to the blade, shield wherever. It turned, so we ran round the pillars to the other side.",
      thermist: "Cold: the floor splits, blade half and light half. Strikers in the light, healer in the blade, shield anywhere. Hot: it turns, and everyone crosses again, round the pillars. The last blow fell on the lot of us.",
      driftblade: "The floor split in two, blade half and light half, and the strikers go to the light and the healer to the blade, and when it turned I was through the middle, round the pillars and across before it finished turning.",
      alembist: "Observed: the floor halved into blade and light. Note: strikers to the light half, healer to the blade half, shield anywhere. The halves turn, so all cross again, round the pillars. Label: a last blow follows for everyone.",
      threadweaver: "The floor split along a seam, blade on one side, light on the other. The strikers sat in the light, I in the blade, our shield anywhere. When the seam turned, we crossed again, round the pillars. The last blow caught us all.",
      marionettist: "(The stage is divided: blade side, light side.) Strikers take the light, the healer the blade, the shield anywhere. When the halves turn, the company crosses again, around the pillars, and a final blow falls on all.",
      cleric: "The floor split into a half of blade and a half of light. The strikers stood in the light, I in the blade, our knight wherever suited. When it turned we crossed again, round the pillars, and the last blow fell on all of us.",
      grovekeeper: "The floor split like cracked ground, a blade half and a light half. The strikers stood in the light, I in the blade, our shield anywhere. When it turned we crossed again, round the pillars. The last blow came for all of us.",
      chronomancer: "The floor splits, blade half and light half, and then splits again the other way. The strikers go to the light, I to the blade, the shield anywhere. We crossed twice, round the pillars, and the last blow came as it always has.",
      tidecaller: "The floor was divided like a shore at low water, blade half and light half. The strikers took the light, I the blade, and our shield stood anywhere. When it turned, we crossed again, round the pillars, and the last blow rolled over all.",
      lanternkeeper: "The floor was split, a blade half and a light half. Strikers in the light, me in the blade, one lamp on each side. When the halves turned we crossed again, round the pillars, and the last blow came for all four.",
      kenseier: "The floor halved into blade and light. The strikers stood in the light, the healer in the blade, and I where I chose. The halves turned, and we crossed on the beat, round the pillars. The last blow came for all.",
      houndmaster: "Floor cut in two, blade half and light half. Strikers in the light, healer in the blade, me and the lads wherever. When it turned we crossed again, round the pillars. Last blow on the lot.",
    } },
    'Last Rites': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "Two coffins closed, one on the healer, one on a striker. The free striker and I cut them open, one then the other. The blade hunted the free striker meanwhile. Whichever opened second had to be mended through the edge of the Burial.",
      gloomsworn: "Two coffins shut, one on the healer, one on a striker. I broke one and the free striker broke the other. A man who has been buried knows which to open first: the healer's. The blade hunted the free striker throughout.",
      thresher: "Two coffins, dear, one for our healer and one for a striker. The free striker and the shield broke them one after the other, and the blade hunted the free striker all the while. The second to open is mended through the final bell.",
      bloodreaver: "Two coffins snapped shut, healer and a striker! I smashed one, the free striker smashed the other. The blade came for the free one, and they danced it. Whoever was opened second bled through the end, and lived.",
      runeguard: "The sign: two coffins, on the healer and on one striker. The shield and the free striker break one, then the other, in that order and no other. The blade follows the free striker meanwhile; the one broken last is healed through the Burial.",
      gorgemaw: "Two guests boxed up for later: the healer and a striker. I cracked one, the free striker cracked the other, with the blade chasing the free one throughout. The second box opens late, and the guest in it must be mended through the last course.",
      oathbroker: "Two parties were sealed: the healer and a striker. The free striker and I breached them in sequence while the blade hunted the free striker. Whoever is breached second bears the closing instalment, and must be mended.",
      ironpalm: "Two coffins closed, on the healer and on a striker. The free striker and I opened them, one and then the other. The blade chased the free striker meanwhile. The second to open bore the last of it, and was mended.",
      ranger: "Two coffins, healer and one striker. Free striker and the shield broke one, then the other. Blade hunted the free striker the whole time. Last one open took the final hit; healed through.",
      shadowblade: "Two coffins, healer and a striker, and the blade came for the free striker, which I disliked, being the one it wanted. I cut one open, then the other, while keeping out of the line. The second had to be mended.",
      pyromancer: "Two coffins shut on the healer and one of us strikers, and the blade came for the free one, which was me! I broke one open between dodges, the shield broke the other. The second out was mended through the end.",
      thermist: "Cold: two coffins, healer and one striker. The free striker and the shield break them, one then the other. Hot: the blade hunts the free striker meanwhile. Whoever opens second is healed through the last edge.",
      driftblade: "Two coffins closed, healer and a striker, and the blade hunted the free striker, me, so I broke one open running and the shield broke the other, and the second out took the last of it, mended through.",
      alembist: "Observed: two coffins, the healer's and a striker's. Note: the free striker and the shield break one, then the other, while the blade hunts the free striker. The second out must be dosed through the Burial's edge.",
      threadweaver: "Two coffins sealed, me and a striker, with Burial ticking over both. The free striker and our shield cut one open, then the other, with the blade chasing. Whichever of us came out second had to be mended through the last stitch.",
      marionettist: "(Two coffins close on the stage: the healer, and a striker.) The free striker and the shield break them in turn, one then the other, the blade chasing the free striker. The second player out takes the curtain's edge.",
      cleric: "I was sealed in a coffin, and so was one of the strikers. The free striker and our knight broke one open and then the other. The blade hunted the free striker. Whoever was opened second took the last of it; I hoped, gladly, to be first.",
      grovekeeper: "A coffin closed on me and another on a striker. The free striker and our shield opened them one after the other, with the blade chasing the free striker. The second out was mended through the last of it. Seeds survive worse.",
      chronomancer: "I was sealed in one coffin, a striker in the other, and the blade came for the free striker. They broke one open, then the other. Whoever was second had to be healed through the end of it. We decided which, in advance.",
      tidecaller: "A coffin shut on me and another on a striker. The free striker and our shield broke them one after the other, with the blade chasing the free striker. The second out was carried through the last swell.",
      lanternkeeper: "Two coffins, mine and a striker's. The free striker and our shield broke one open, then the other, with the blade chasing the free striker. Whichever lamp is lit second must be kept burning through the end.",
      kenseier: "Two coffins, on the healer and a striker. The free striker and I cut them open in order, one and then the other, while the blade hunted the free striker. The second was healed through the final stroke.",
      houndmaster: "Two coffins, healer and a striker. Free striker and the shield-man broke them one after the other, blade at the free one's heels. Second one out took the last knock and was mended. Easy now.",
    } },
    'Hollowing': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "The Seraph closed its wings and everyone took the frost at once, no ground to choose. I stood by the healer. Then the second blow was coming, and the healer had to top us all up before it landed.",
      gloomsworn: "The wings closed round it and the cold came for all of us together. There was nowhere to stand. We drew close to the healer and were mended before the second blow, which was heavier than the first.",
      thresher: "The wings folded, dear, and a great frost came for all of us at once, and then a second blow a moment after. Stay close to the healer and be mended in between. It is all in the gap.",
      bloodreaver: "It folded its wings and the cold hit all four of us at once, hard! Nothing to do but take it. Then the second blow, a heavier one, and we huddled by the healer to get mended in the gap.",
      runeguard: "The sign: the wings close, and a great frost falls on all four at once, with a heavier blow to follow. No ground is safe; the order is simply to gather by the healer and be mended between the first and the second.",
      gorgemaw: "The wings closed like a lid, and the frost came down on every plate at once. No side dish for this. We clustered by the healer, got mended, and met the second blow, which came heavier, well fed.",
      oathbroker: "The wings are furled, and a frost is levied on all four parties at once, with a heavier sum due soon after. There is no clause of exemption. We gathered by the healer, and were mended in the interval.",
      ironpalm: "The wings closed and the frost spoke to us all at once, then once more, harder. There was nowhere to stand apart. We gathered by the healer and were mended in the pause between.",
      ranger: "Wings shut, frost on all four at once. Nowhere to stand. Second blow harder, close behind. Went to the healer, got mended in the gap.",
      shadowblade: "It shut its wings and the cold found all of us at once, even me, which was rude. No shade helped. We gathered by the healer and were mended in the pause before the second blow, which was heavier.",
      pyromancer: "It closed those magnificent wings and froze all four of us at once! No hiding anywhere, so I huddled by the healer, and got mended in the pause before the second blow, which was larger than the first.",
      thermist: "Cold, all at once: the wings close and the frost takes all four of us. Hot: the second blow, heavier. Nothing to dodge, so I went to the healer and was mended in the gap between.",
      driftblade: "The wings shut and the frost came for all of us at once and there was nowhere to run, which I hate, so I went to the healer and stood still just long enough to be mended before the second blow.",
      alembist: "Observed: wings closed, frost on all four at once, then a heavier blow soon after. Note: no ground is safe. Everyone gathers by the healer, and the dose goes in during the gap between the two.",
      threadweaver: "The wings shut and the frost took all four of us at once, a heavier blow following. No seam to cut. I gathered my stitches close and mended all of them in the gap between.",
      marionettist: "(The wings close; the frost falls upon the whole company at once, and a heavier blow follows.) No blocking to be done. The company gathered by the healer and was mended in the interval.",
      cleric: "The wings closed and the frost took all four of us at once, a heavier blow close behind. There was nowhere to hide, so I drew everyone close and mended them in the gap between, before the second blow came.",
      grovekeeper: "The wings shut like a cloud closing, and the frost came on all four of us together, a harder blow close behind. No shelter. My lot gathered by me and I mended them in the quiet between.",
      chronomancer: "The wings close, the frost falls on us all together, then a heavier blow a little after. Nothing to step out of. I gathered everyone close and healed them all in the gap, which is the only room there is.",
      tidecaller: "The wings closed and a cold swell came over all four of us at once, a harder one behind it. No high ground. We gathered close, and I raised the water in the gap between the two.",
      lanternkeeper: "The wings shut and the frost came on all four of us at once, a heavier blow behind it. No lamp can stop it. I drew everyone in and topped up every wick in the gap between.",
      kenseier: "The wings closed. Frost fell on all four of us at once, with a heavier blow close after. Steel is no use against a cold like that. We drew in beside the healer and were mended in the gap between.",
      houndmaster: "Wings shut, frost on all of us at once, heavier blow after. Whistled the lads in tight by the healer and got mended in the gap. No sidestepping that one.",
    } },
    'Cold Sermon': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "Beams ran from the halo to every pillar, and every pillar cast a red lane straight away from the Seraph to the wall. I stood off every lane, and the lanes fired twice. The ground behind a pillar was the worst ground in the court.",
      gloomsworn: "Each pillar cast a red lane away from the Seraph, to the wall, and cast it twice. The ground behind a pillar, which had been shelter all night, was the worst place to be. I stood between the lanes.",
      thresher: "Every pillar sang out, dear, and threw a red lane straight away from the Seraph to the wall, and again a moment after. The ground behind a pillar is quite the wrong spot now. Stand between the lanes.",
      bloodreaver: "Every pillar lit red and shot a lane straight back from the big one to the wall, and shot it twice! The ground behind a pillar, the safe spot all night, was the worst. I stood between the lanes.",
      runeguard: "The sign: beams run from the broken ring to each pillar. The remedy: each pillar casts a lane straight away from the Seraph, to the wall, and again soon after. The shelter behind a pillar is now the lane. We stood between them.",
      gorgemaw: "Each pillar served a red lane straight away from the Seraph to the wall, and served it twice. Behind a pillar had been a quiet seat all night; now it was the worst. We sat between the lanes.",
      oathbroker: "Each pillar now enforces a red lane running straight away from the Seraph to the wall, and enforces it twice. The ground behind a pillar, once sheltered, is the place of liability. We took the gaps instead.",
      ironpalm: "Each pillar spoke, and a red lane ran from it to the wall, away from the Seraph, and again soon after. Behind a pillar had been refuge. Now it was the loudest place. I stood between the lanes.",
      ranger: "Each pillar throws a lane, straight back from the Seraph to the wall, twice. Behind a pillar is now the worst ground. Stood between lanes.",
      shadowblade: "Each pillar cast a lane of red straight away from the mark to the wall, and again after. The shade behind a pillar, my favourite place all night, became the worst place to be. I stood between the lanes.",
      pyromancer: "Each pillar I'd relied on turned traitor and cast a red lane straight away from the Seraph to the wall, twice! The shade behind a pillar was suddenly the brightest spot. I stood between the lanes and fumed.",
      thermist: "Cold: each pillar casts a red lane away from the Seraph to the wall. Hot: it casts it twice, the second harder. Behind a pillar is the worst place now. I stood between the lanes.",
      driftblade: "Each pillar fired a red lane straight away from the Seraph, to the wall, and again, and I stood between the lanes and slipped through the gaps, since behind the pillars, where I had hidden all night, was now the worst place.",
      alembist: "Observed: each pillar casts a red lane straight away from the Seraph to the wall, then again. Note: behind a pillar was shelter, and is now the lane. Stand between the lanes; label the pillars as hazards.",
      threadweaver: "Every pillar pulled a red thread straight out from the Seraph to the wall, twice. Behind a pillar had been my hiding seam; now it was the snag. I kept my stitches between the lanes.",
      marionettist: "(Each pillar casts a red lane from the star to the wall, and again.) The scenery turned on the company. Behind a pillar was the worst place to be. We took our marks between the lanes.",
      cleric: "Each pillar cast a red lane straight away from the Seraph to the wall, twice. The ground behind a pillar, which had sheltered us, was the worst ground. I asked all of them to stand between the lanes.",
      grovekeeper: "Each pillar threw a red lane straight away from the Seraph to the wall, twice, like frost running along a fence. The ground behind a pillar was no longer shade. My lot stood between the lanes.",
      chronomancer: "Each pillar casts a lane, straight away from the Seraph, and then casts it again, so the second is the one that finishes you. The ground behind a pillar was shelter earlier. Stand between the lanes.",
      tidecaller: "Every pillar sent a red lane out from the Seraph to the wall, like a rip off a headland, twice. The ground behind a pillar, quiet water all night, was the worst of it. We stood between the lanes.",
      lanternkeeper: "Every pillar cast a red lane straight away from the Seraph, to the wall, twice. The ground behind a pillar, which had been the lit side, was now the worst. Four of us, all between the lanes.",
      kenseier: "Each pillar cast a lane straight away from the Seraph to the wall, and again on the second beat. Behind stone had been shelter; it was now the lane. A blade cannot turn it, so we stood between the lanes.",
      houndmaster: "Every pillar threw a red lane straight back from the big lad to the wall, twice. Behind a pillar's no place to be now. Kept the lads and myself in the gaps.",
    } },
    'Six Wings': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "A wing lifted for each beat. A cone at a striker, a circle on the healer, a blade through a striker, a toll on the healer which I took standing in the ring, a ring about the Seraph with a quiet middle, then the throw to the walls.",
      gloomsworn: "Six wings, six beats. A cone, a circle, a blade, a toll I took from the ring beside the healer, a ring round the Seraph with a quiet middle, then the throw to the walls. I took my part of each as it came.",
      thresher: "Six wings, dear, and a lifted wing for each little step: a cone, a circle, a blade, a toll, a ring with a quiet middle, and the great throw to the walls. Our shield took the toll from the ring. Quite a dance.",
      bloodreaver: "Six wings lifted, six blows, and I loved every one! The cone, the circle, the blade through a striker, the toll on the healer that I took standing in the ring, the ring round the big one, and last the throw to the walls.",
      runeguard: "The sign: a wing lifts, and then a beat. The order: cone at a striker, circle on the healer, a blade through a striker, a toll on the healer which the shield takes from the ring, a ring round the Seraph, then the throw to the walls.",
      gorgemaw: "Six wings, six courses. A cone for a striker, a circle for the healer, a blade for a striker, a toll for the healer that I took from the ring, a ring round the host with a quiet middle, and the throw to the walls.",
      oathbroker: "Six wings, six clauses, in fixed order: a cone to a striker, a circle to the healer, a blade through a striker, a toll on the healer which I countered from the ring, a ring about the Seraph, and the throw to the walls.",
      ironpalm: "A wing lifted, and a beat followed, six times. A cone, a circle, a blade, a toll that I took from the ring, a ring with a quiet middle, the throw to the walls. I answered each as it came.",
      ranger: "Six wings, six beats. Cone at a striker, circle on the healer, blade through a striker, toll on the healer with the shield in the ring, ring round the Seraph, then thrown to the walls. Read the wing, move on the beat.",
      shadowblade: "A wing lifted for each beat, and each beat named whom it wanted. A cone for a striker, a circle for the healer, a blade for a striker, a toll for the healer, a ring about the mark with a quiet middle, then the throw to the walls.",
      pyromancer: "Six beats, a wing for each, like a show with no intermission! Cone at a striker, circle on the healer, blade through a striker, a toll on the healer, a ring round the Seraph with a quiet middle, and the throw to the walls.",
      thermist: "Cold, in order: a wing lifts, then a beat. Cone at a striker, circle on the healer, blade through a striker, toll on the healer, ring round the Seraph. Hot, last: the throw to the walls. Open floor behind me, and I rode it.",
      driftblade: "Six wings, six beats, and I moved through all of them: out of the cone, away from the circle, wide of the blade line, round the toll, into the quiet middle of the ring, and then I flew with the throw to the walls.",
      alembist: "Observed: a wing lifts for each beat, six in all. Cone at a striker, circle on the healer, blade through a striker, toll on the healer, ring round the Seraph with a quiet middle, then the throw to the walls. Note: read the wing.",
      threadweaver: "Six wings, and a seam to mind for each. A cone on a striker, a circle on me, a blade through a striker, a toll our shield took from the ring, a ring round the Seraph, then the throw. I led my circle off the hem.",
      marionettist: "(Six wings, six cues.) A cone at a striker, a circle on the healer, a blade through a striker, a toll on the healer, a ring round the star with a quiet middle, and the throw to the walls. The company hit every mark.",
      cleric: "A wing lifted for each of six beats: a cone at a striker, a circle on me, a blade through a striker, a toll that our knight took from the ring, a ring about the Seraph, then the throw. I walked the circle out of the way.",
      grovekeeper: "Six wings lifted in turn, like a field turning over. A cone, a circle on me, a blade through a striker, a toll our shield took from the ring, a ring with a quiet middle, then the throw to the walls. I led my circle off.",
      chronomancer: "A wing lifts, a beat falls, six times: cone, circle on me, blade, toll, ring, throw. Our shield took the toll from the ring beside me. I walked my circle off before it landed.",
      tidecaller: "Six wings lifted, one after another, like six waves in a set. Cone at a striker, circle on me, blade through a striker, toll on me that our shield took from the ring, a ring round the Seraph, then the throw to the walls.",
      lanternkeeper: "A wing lifted for each beat, six in all. Cone, circle on me, blade, toll on me with our shield in the ring, a ring round the Seraph with a quiet middle, then the throw. I walked my circle clear of the others.",
      kenseier: "Six wings, six beats, and every one countable: a cone at a striker, a circle on the healer, a blade through a striker, a toll I took from the ring, a ring about the Seraph, the throw. I stepped through the ring's quiet middle.",
      houndmaster: "Wing lifts, beat follows, six times over. Cone at a striker, circle on the healer, blade through a striker, a toll the shield-man took in the ring, a ring round the big lad, then the throw. Read the wing, lads.",
    } },
    'The Unsaid': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "The last blow struck all four of us, and every pillar still standing burst in a red ring. I stood clear of them. We were healed full beforehand, and had broken or left few pillars. Too much cover is a mistake.",
      gloomsworn: "The last blow fell on all four of us at once, and every pillar left standing burst in a red ring round itself. I stood far from every one. The healer had us full before it. Cover is only kind while it lasts.",
      thresher: "The last blow, dear: all four of us at once, and every pillar still standing bursts in a red ring. Keep well away from them, and be healed to the brim first. Too much shelter has a price.",
      bloodreaver: "The last blow hit all four of us at once, and every pillar still standing burst in a red ring! I stood clear of them all, and we were healed to the brim first. Too many pillars would have been too many scars.",
      runeguard: "The sign: the last blow, on all four at once, and every pillar still standing bursts in a red ring about itself. The remedy: be healed to the full beforehand, and stand clear of what remains. Cover kept is cover owed.",
      gorgemaw: "The last course fell on all four of us at once, and every pillar still standing burst like an overfilled pastry in a red ring. I stood clear of them all, topped up beforehand. Too much shelter, and one is served it.",
      oathbroker: "The final charge falls on all four parties at once, and every pillar still standing is forfeit in a red ring about itself. We were healed in full beforehand and stood clear of what remained. Surplus cover is a liability.",
      ironpalm: "The last blow came for all four of us, and each pillar still standing burst in a red ring. I stood far from them, healed full beforehand. The more cover we kept, the more it answered at the end.",
      ranger: "Last blow on all four, and every pillar still standing burst in a red ring. Stood well clear of them. Healed full before it, no spare cover left to hurt us.",
      shadowblade: "The last blow fell on all four of us, and every pillar left standing burst in a red ring. The shade I'd loved all night turned on me. I stayed well clear of all of them, and was healed full beforehand.",
      pyromancer: "The last blow hit all four of us, and every pillar left standing burst in a red ring! My dear shade, turned against me. I stood well clear and arrived fully healed. Cover is a wonderful thing to be sentimental about.",
      thermist: "Cold: the last blow comes for all four of us. Hot: every pillar still standing bursts in a red ring. I stood clear of them all and was healed to the brim first. Too many pillars, too much heat.",
      driftblade: "The last blow hit all four of us and every pillar left standing burst in a red ring, so I was well away from all of them by then, through the gaps and out, and fully healed before it.",
      alembist: "Observed: the last blow on all four, and a red ring from every pillar left standing. Note: be fully dosed beforehand, and stay clear of the pillars. Label it plainly: too much cover is a hazard.",
      threadweaver: "The last blow fell on all four of us at once, and each pillar still standing burst in a red ring. I had everyone mended to the brim first, and they stood clear. Too many seams left open, in the end.",
      marionettist: "(The final blow strikes the whole company; every pillar still standing bursts in a red ring.) We were healed in advance and stood clear of the scenery. A party that keeps too much scenery loses the final scene.",
      cleric: "The last blow came for all four of us, and every pillar left standing burst in a red ring. I had everyone healed to the brim beforehand, and asked them to stand clear. Too much shelter has its cost.",
      grovekeeper: "The last blow fell on all four of us, and every pillar still standing burst in a red ring like a seed pod. I had my lot full before it and standing well clear. Too much shade, in the end, had a cost.",
      chronomancer: "The last blow falls on all four of us, and each pillar still standing bursts in a red ring. I had everyone healed to the brim first and clear of the pillars. Too many left standing, and it ends sooner than you'd like.",
      tidecaller: "The last swell broke on all four of us, and every pillar still standing burst in a red ring, like spray off a rock. I had the water high in everyone first, and we stood clear. Too many rocks on the shore, in the end.",
      lanternkeeper: "The last blow fell on all four of us, and each pillar still standing burst in a red ring. I topped up every wick first and we stood clear of the pillars. Four of us, and no more cover than we could walk away from.",
      kenseier: "The last blow fell on all four of us. Nothing in my hands could answer it. Every pillar still standing burst in a red ring, so we stood clear, healed to the full. Stone kept too long becomes a hazard.",
      houndmaster: "Last blow on all four of us, and every pillar left standing burst in a red ring. Whistled the lads clear of every one, healed up first. Too much cover and he gets you at the end.",
    } },
  },
};
